You are auditing a repair pass of the Harn release flow for an
existing open Release PR (`{{ fixup_pr_url }}`). The harness recovered
the original pin SHA via `git merge-base origin/release/v{{ target_version }} origin/{{ base_branch }}`
and used pin-time `## Unreleased` (read from that commit's CHANGELOG.md)
as the authoritative description of v{{ target_version }}. This re-run
exists either because the original ship-pr left the PR open and we are
correcting content (e.g., a truncated CHANGELOG) or because post-publish
drift has accumulated on `{{ base_branch }}` and the PR needs to catch up.

What the harness already did, deterministically:

- Force-pushed the release branch onto a fresh `{{ base_branch }}`
  snapshot so any merges from other sessions flow through.
- Promoted pin-time `## Unreleased` into `## v{{ target_version }}`
  above the next-older version heading.
- **Smart-subtracted the pin-time bullets from the current Unreleased.**
  When pin-time content is a contiguous substring of current Unreleased
  (the common append-only case), the harness removed it cleanly so
  Unreleased holds only post-pin drift. When the current Unreleased was
  edited rather than just appended-to, the harness preserved both
  verbatim — duplicate bullets are possible and the operator may need
  to dedupe by hand.
- Skipped audit / dry-run / re-tagging where origin already proves
  those gates passed (CI re-runs the same gates on the merge queue;
  the tag — if it exists — was pushed during the original publish and
  must not move).

Constraints — non-negotiable:

- If `v{{ target_version }}` already shipped, the tag stays where it is.
  Do not recommend retagging, force-pushing, or moving it. Re-shipping
  a published version is impossible (crates.io is immutable).
- Do not author a new release section. Pin-time `## Unreleased` is
  authoritative for v{{ target_version }} content.
- Do not recommend reverting the smart-subtract — post-pin drift in
  the current Unreleased describes work landing AFTER this release,
  not in it.

Your job: a tight verification pass. Use only local read-only tools.
Inspect the merged CHANGELOG.md and at least one PR/diff/file source.
Then return a short Audit block.

Confirm:

- The promoted v{{ target_version }} body matches pin-time Unreleased
  with no obvious truncation, dropped bullets, or mid-sentence cuts.
- `## Unreleased` either is empty (clean subtract) or contains only
  bullets that genuinely describe post-pin work landing AFTER this
  release.

Flag, if any:

- v{{ target_version }} bullets that look truncated or mid-sentence.
- Unreleased bullets that look like duplicates of v{{ target_version }}
  bullets (the smart-subtract failed and the operator should dedupe
  before merge).
- Anything in v{{ target_version }} that contradicts what the published
  tag (if it exists) actually delivered.

Do not include `BEGIN_DRAFT_CHANGELOG` markers.
